{"q":"41","t":"First Missing Positive","d":"Hard","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an unsorted integer array <code>nums</code>. Return the <em>smallest positive integer</em> that is <em>not present</em> in <code>nums</code>.</p>\n\n<p>You must implement an algorithm that runs in <code>O(n)</code> time and uses <code>O(1)</code> auxiliary space.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,2,0]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The numbers in the range [1,2] are all in the array.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums = [3,4,-1,1]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> 1 is in the array but 2 is missing.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums = [7,8,9,11,12]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The smallest positive integer 1 is missing.\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>-2<sup>31</sup> &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":["Think about how you would solve the problem in non-constant space.  Can you apply that logic to the existing space?","We don't care about duplicates or non-positive integers","Remember that O(2n) = O(n)"],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"firstMissingPositive\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Hash Table","slug":"hash-table"}],"s":[{"t":"Missing Number","s":"missing-number","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Find the Duplicate Number","s":"find-the-duplicate-number","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Find All Numbers Disappeared in an Array","s":"find-all-numbers-disappeared-in-an-array","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Couples Holding Hands","s":"couples-holding-hands","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Smallest Number in Infinite Set","s":"smallest-number-in-infinite-set","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Number of Integers to Choose From a Range I","s":"maximum-number-of-integers-to-choose-from-a-range-i","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Smallest Missing Non-negative Integer After Operations","s":"smallest-missing-non-negative-integer-after-operations","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Number of Integers to Choose From a Range II","s":"maximum-number-of-integers-to-choose-from-a-range-ii","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Smallest Missing Integer Greater Than Sequential Prefix Sum","s":"smallest-missing-integer-greater-than-sequential-prefix-sum","d":"Easy","p":false}],"co":[["Google","google"],["Amazon","amazon"],["tcs","tcs"],["Meta","facebook"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Zoho","zoho"],["Oracle","oracle"],["MakeMyTrip","makemytrip"],["Netflix","netflix"],["Myntra","myntra"],["Zomato","zomato"],["Cognizant","cognizant"],["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs"],["Tesla","tesla"],["Salesforce","salesforce"],["Nutanix","nutanix"],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs"],["ServiceNow","servicenow"],["Nvidia","nvidia"],["General Motors","general-motors"],["Swiggy","swiggy"]],"cs":{"a":[["tcs","tcs",14],["Google","google",11],["Amazon","amazon",9],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",2]],"b":[["Meta","facebook",4],["Microsoft","microsoft",2],["Zoho","zoho",2]],"m":[["Oracle","oracle",7],["ServiceNow","servicenow",5],["MakeMyTrip","makemytrip",5],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs",4],["Netflix","netflix",4],["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs",3],["EPAM Systems","epam-systems",3],["Cognizant","cognizant",3],["Geico","geico",3],["Tesla","tesla",2]]}}